Dominant Pairs
Difficulty: EasyAccuracy: 50.57%Submissions: 43K+Points: 2
Given an even-sized integer array arr[], count the number of dominant pairs. A pair of indices (i, j) is called dominant if all of the following conditions hold:

0 ≤ i < arr.size() / 2
arr.size() / 2 ≤ j < arr.size() 
arr[i] ≥ 5 × arr[j] 
Return the total number of dominant pairs.


Note: 0-based indexing is used.











class Solution {
	public:
	int dominantPairs(vector<int> &arr) {
		// Code here
		int n = arr.size();
		int result = 0;
		int mid = n>> 1;
		sort(arr.begin(), arr.begin() + mid);
		sort(arr.begin() + mid, arr.end());
		int right = mid;
		for (int left = 0; left<mid; ++left) {
			while (right<n && arr[left] >= 5*arr[right])right++;
			result += (right - mid);
		}
		return result;
	}
};
